                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fda49c1e-0c57-492a-a2e6-ebb17aac456f",
                        "source_entry_id": "604cfbac-e9a8-3882-9461-9382b1ac8af0",
                        "source_sense_id": "dd99c75f-67cb-387a-8f74-efdc2b5c4357",
                        "target_lang_word": "agon",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "agon",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf100b8f-daf2-356b-9c2d-73603818039f",
                                        "entry_id": "381bd75a-517e-369d-a024-f6fccdf4fae0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A struggle or contest; conflict; especially between the protagonist and antagonist in a literary work."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b4eb1b5-0852-4ac0-96f8-a4c738a99e38",
                                                "sense_id": "cf100b8f-daf2-356b-9c2d-73603818039f",
                                                "text": "It was not ecological pressure or shortages of protein, as anthropologist Marvin Harris has claimed; institutionalized violence, as opposed to the stylized agons of hunters over grievances, was the shadow side of the Neolithic Revolution."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8e8342c-5fa1-45bd-893d-d85fafeac81b",
                                                "sense_id": "cf100b8f-daf2-356b-9c2d-73603818039f",
                                                "text": "One way of reading Beowulf is to think of it as three agons in the hero's life[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b76aca9-31eb-4d67-9e45-0c31a1cdf2db",
                                                "sense_id": "cf100b8f-daf2-356b-9c2d-73603818039f",
                                                "text": "The other ethical system is that of agon. Agon is a battlefield. We enter agon not to exchange, but to fight. We dream of winning but are also prepared to lose – including to lose ourselves, even in the literal sense of dying for a great cause."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d52b027e-d934-385b-9da0-0bcde90c38fb",
                                        "entry_id": "381bd75a-517e-369d-a024-f6fccdf4fae0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An intellectual conflict or apparent competition of ideas."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1118a299-9f58-4c24-b5a4-a6c534bb45f1",
                                                "sense_id": "d52b027e-d934-385b-9da0-0bcde90c38fb",
                                                "text": "Freud's originality stemmed from his aggression and ambition in his agon with biology."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd84770d-14cf-461a-b4ce-e48cb45eaf85",
                                                "sense_id": "d52b027e-d934-385b-9da0-0bcde90c38fb",
                                                "text": "The point, though, is that to fully and uncritically surrender to such agon against individuals is to invite one's own ethical degeneration; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43e9527c-f339-39b5-b0ab-2b3578ccc975",
                                        "entry_id": "381bd75a-517e-369d-a024-f6fccdf4fae0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A contest in ancient Greece, as in athletics or music, in which prizes were awarded."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "503922c0-04b1-3548-86a6-68c4cce4ab94",
                                        "entry_id": "381bd75a-517e-369d-a024-f6fccdf4fae0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A two-player board game played on a hexagonally-tiled board, popular in Victorian times."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
